=== Prompt for HW-002 (attempt 1) ===
Implement user story HW-002: Verify all tests pass

## Story Description
Run the project test suite using the Node 20 vitest binary and confirm all 3 vitest tests in greet.test.ts pass. This is a read-only verification story: do not modify, create, or delete any files. Capture the complete combined stdout/stderr of the vitest run and report it verbatim (unedited, untruncated) in the story report, along with the observed exit code and the before/after git cleanliness checks.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Tests are executed with exactly: ~/.local/share/fnm/node-versions/v20.20.2/installation/bin/node ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run (tilde resolved to $HOME; no additional flags, no --max-turns-style wrappers, no watch mode)
- The vitest process terminates with exit code 0, captured immediately after the run via $? (or equivalent) and stated explicitly in the story report
- The captured output contains the literal line fragment 'Test Files  1 passed (1)'
- The captured output contains the literal line fragment 'Tests  3 passed (3)'
- The test result summary lines contain no 'failed', 'skipped', 'todo', or 'only' counts — i.e., zero tests in any state other than passed
- Immediately before the vitest run, 'git status --porcelain -- src/ tests/ test/ *.test.* vitest.config.*' (restricted to tracked source, test, and test-config paths) produces empty output, and the identical command produces empty output immediately after the run, demonstrating no files were modified by this story
- The full, unedited, untruncated combined stdout/stderr of the vitest run is included verbatim in the story report as a single fenced block
- No file is created, modified, or deleted by this story; only read-only and process-execution operations are performed

